## Two Real Systems We Stock: AUDIX Wireless Lavalier Sets and the AUDIX HT5 Headband Mic

Our hands free microphone inventory is two distinct products, not one item sold under two names. The first is the AUDIX RAD-360 wireless lavalier set, and we own two complete units of it. Each set is a full wireless chain: a receiver, a bodypack transmitter, a lavalier capsule that clips to a lapel or collar, and 2 antennas. Two complete sets means two people can wear one at the same time, an officiant and a second presenter, or two panelists, run through the same receiver setup our technician manages on site.

The second is the AUDIX HT5, a wireless headband mic, sometimes called a diadema mic. We own one of these. It is a genuinely different piece of hardware from the lavalier sets above, not a clip on capsule but a small boom that curves from behind the ear to sit close to the corner of the mouth.

We are being precise here on purpose. Our equipment catalog also lists a spare bodypack transmitter and a spare lavalier capsule as loose components alongside this inventory. We have not confirmed whether those spares combine with the HT5 headband to form a third simultaneous wireless channel, so we do not offer that as a booking option here. What we can confirm and book today is two complete lavalier sets and one headband mic, as separate real items.

